          "title": "Finding a Unit Vector Parallel to a Vector Sum"
        },
        "question": {
          ":question/id": "b1c99578-547d-5a2b-9e59-c370944ac960",
          ":question/problem": "The vector $a$ is directed due south-west and $|a|=8$, while the vector $b$ is directed due north-west and $|b|=4.$ Which of the following is a unit vector that is parallel to $a+b?$",
          ":question/worked-solution": "First, we have to find $a+b.$ According to the triangle law of addition, the resultant $a+b$ goes from the tail of $a$ to the head of $b:$\n\n![](/tmp/ca9837-templates-5ek4tgt5/17592186096815/sum-b0790380872b09bfb3c8da3f.png)\n\nTo find the unit vector corresponding to $a+b,$ we have to divide by the magnitude:\n\n$$\nu=\\frac{a+b}{|a+b|}\n$$\n\nThe given directions are perpendicular, so we obtain a right triangle. We can use the Pythagorean theorem:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|a+b|^2&=|a|^2+|b|^2\\\\\n&=(8)^2+(4)^2\\\\\n&=64+16\\\\\n&=80\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the magnitude is\n\n$$\n|a+b|=\\sqrt{80}=4 \\sqrt{5}\n$$\n\nand the corresponding unit vector is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u&=\\frac{a+b}{|a+b|}\\\\\n&=\\frac{1}{4 \\sqrt{5}}(a+b).\\end{aligned}\n$$",
          ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/hard",
